---
title: Butter chicken
servings: 4
tags: [indian, chicken, make-ahead]
cuisine: indian
time: 35 minutes, plus 3 hours marinating
source: Butter Chicken by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/butter-chicken/
---

In a bowl, mix the @plain yogurt{1/2%cup}(full-fat), @lemon juice{1%tbsp},
@ground turmeric{1%tsp}, @garam masala{2%tsp}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp},
@ground cumin{1%tsp}, @ginger{1%tbsp}(freshly grated) and
@garlic{2%cloves}(crushed).

Stir in the @chicken thighs{750%g}(boneless skinless, bite-size pieces). Cover
and refrigerate ~{3%hours} to ~{24%hours}; overnight is best.

Heat the @ghee{2%tbsp}(or butter) in a large #frying pan{} over high heat.
Lift the chicken out of the bowl, leaving the leftover marinade behind but not
wiping the pieces. Cook ~{3%minutes}, until white all over. It won't brown
much.

Add the @tomato puree{1%cup}(passata), @heavy cream{1%cup},
@granulated sugar{1%tbsp}, @salt{1 1/4%tsp} and the marinade left in the bowl.

Turn the heat to low and simmer ~{20%minutes}. Taste for salt.

Scatter with @cilantro{} and serve with @basmati rice{}.

> Use pure ground chili or cayenne for the heat, not an American chili powder blend.
